Core plugin implementation (REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE, REQ-RULE-REGISTRY, REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM, REQ-ERROR-HANDLING, REQ-TYPESCRIPT):
- File: src/index.ts
  /** @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE @req REQ-ERROR-HANDLING */
  - Dynamic rule registry:
    const RULE_NAMES = ["require-story-annotation","require-req-annotation","require-branch-annotation","valid-annotation-format","valid-story-reference","valid-req-reference","prefer-implements-annotation"] as const;
    const rules: Record = {} as any;
    RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => {
      try {
        const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
        rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
      } catch (error: any) {
        console.error(`[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`);
        rules[name] = { meta: { type: "problem", docs: { description: `Failed to load rule '${name}'` }, schema: [] }, create(context) { return { Program(node) { context.report({ node, message: `eslint-plugin-traceability: Error loading rule "${name}": ${error.message}` }); } }; } } as Rule.RuleModule;
      }
    });
  - Flat-config presets:
    const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES = {
      "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
      "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
      "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error"
    } as const;
    function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() { return { rules: { ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES } }; }
    const configs = { recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()], strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()] };
    const plugin = { rules, configs, maintenance };
    export { rules, configs, maintenance }; export default plugin;
  - Implemented in TypeScript; tsconfig.json compiles src to lib/ with declarations (REQ-TYPESCRIPT, REQ-NPM-PACKAGE).

ESLint v9 flat-config integration (REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT, Core Functionality):
- File: eslint.config.js
  - Uses flat-config array via module.exports = [...].
  - Dynamically loads the plugin from ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js, with CI-only hard failure and local-dev warning fallback.
  - Registers plugin under traceability when plugin.rules exists:
    plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) }
  - This config is used by CLI tests which call eslint with: --no-config-lookup --config eslint.config.js --stdin ... --rule traceability/require-....

Tests validating plugin structure, registry, configs, and CLI behavior (REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE, REQ-RULE-REGISTRY, REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM, REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT, REQ-ERROR-HANDLING):
- tests/plugin-setup.test.ts:
  /** @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE */
  import plugin, { rules, configs } from "../src/index";
  it("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] plugin exports rules and configs", () => {
    expect(rules).toBeDefined(); expect(configs).toBeDefined();
    expect(typeof rules).toBe("object"); expect(typeof configs).toBe("object");
    expect(plugin.rules).toBe(rules); expect(plugin.configs).toBe(configs);
  });

- tests/plugin-default-export-and-configs.test.ts:
  /** @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md */
  it("[REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE] rules object has correct rule names", () => {
    const expected = ["require-story-annotation","require-req-annotation","require-branch-annotation","valid-annotation-format","valid-story-reference","valid-req-reference","prefer-implements-annotation"];
    const actual = Object.keys(rules);
    expect(actual).toEqual(expected);
  });
  it("[REQ-RULE-REGISTRY] configs.recommended contains correct rule configuration", () => {
    const recommendedRules = configs.recommended[0].rules;
    expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-story-annotation","error");
    expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-req-annotation","error");
    expect(recommendedRules).toHaveProperty("traceability/require-branch-annotation","error");
  });
  it("[REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM] configs.strict contains same rules as recommended", () => {
    const strictRules = configs.strict[0].rules;
    expect(strictRules).toEqual(configs.recommended[0].rules);
  });

- tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts:
  /** @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE - Validate plugin registers via CLI */
  - Spawns ESLint v9 CLI with eslintCliPath, --config eslint.config.js, and various traceability rules; asserts exitStatus matches expectations when annotations are present/missing, demonstrating working flat-config and plugin integration.

Error handling (REQ-ERROR-HANDLING, acceptance criterion ticked in story):
- src/index.ts: rule loader catches require errors, logs to console.error, and installs a placeholder rule that reports a diagnostic instead of throwing.
- tests/plugin-setup-error.test.ts:
  - Mocks ../src/rules/require-branch-annotation to throw; requires ../src/index; asserts console.error contains 'Failed to load rule "require-branch-annotation": Test load error'; verifies placeholder rule meta.docs.description mentions the failure and that its create() function reports an error via context.report.
- tests/cli-error-handling.test.ts:
  - Spawns ESLint CLI with traceability/require-story-annotation rule and a function missing @story; asserts non-zero exit code and error message about missing @story annotation, confirming CLI error path works correctly with the plugin and config.

